11
00:49:15,652 --> 00:49:21,652
Written and directed by M.

12
00:53:44,347 --> 00:53:50,347
Night Shyamalan, the film stars Noah Ringer, Dev Patel, Nicola Peltz,
Jackson Rathbone, Shaun Toub, Aasif Mandvi, and Cliff Curtis.

13
00:58:13,043 --> 00:58:19,043
The plot follows Aang, a young Avatar who must master all four elements of air, water, fire, and earth and restore
balance to the world while stopping the Fire Nation from conquering the Water Tribes and the Earth Kingdom.

14
01:02:41,739 --> 01:02:47,739
Development for the film began in January 2007, with
casting and pre-production taking place in 2008.

15
01:07:10,434 --> 01:07:16,434
Principal photography began in March 2009 and ended in September, with two weeks' shooting in Greenland,
and the rest of the film being shot in various locations in Pennsylvania, United States.

16
01:11:39,130 --> 01:11:45,130
Post-production began in August and took several months
due to the extensive visual effects.

17
01:16:07,826 --> 01:16:13,826
The name Avatar was dropped from the title to avoid
confusion with James Cameron's 2009 film, Avatar.

18
01:20:36,521 --> 01:20:42,521
The Last Airbender premiered at the Alice Tully Hall in New York City on June 30, 2010, and was
theatrically released in the United States the following day by Paramount Pictures.

19
01:25:05,217 --> 01:25:11,217
The film was panned by critics, and is considered to
be one of the worst films of all time.

20
01:29:33,913 --> 01:29:39,913
It grossed $320 million on a $150 million budget, and was
considered to be a box-office disappointment.

21
01:34:02,608 --> 01:34:08,608
The Last Airbender was originally envisioned as a trilogy, each reflecting the show's three seasons, but its
negative reception and poor financial performance led to Nickelodeon cancelling the plans.

22
01:38:31,304 --> 01:38:37,304
The film explores themes of fire, kingdom, war ship, village, prince.
